; Assembler 1.1
; =============
; DEFINE directives, generated symbols, and named function locals.
; The WASI Preview 1 CLI and low-level WAL syntax from 1.0 are retained.
;
; Build with 1.0:
;   wasmtime run --dir . Assembler/bin/assembler.1.0.wal.wasm Assembler/assembler.1.1.wal Assembler/bin/assembler.1.1.wal.wasm
; Run:
;   wasmtime run --dir . Assembler/bin/assembler.1.1.wal.wasm input.wal output.wasm
;
; What's new
; ----------
; DEFINE directives write section entries and maintain their counts.
; Function and memory imports have separate zero-based index spaces.
; Parameters and locals receive indices in declaration order; their symbols
; are removed at code_end. Each function starts with fresh local indices.
; Integer const symbols use signed LEB128; indices and lengths use ULEB128.
; Reassigning #name updates its value. New errors explain DEFINE syntax.
; Active data offsets are signed; passive data has no offset expression.
;
; Directive reference
; -------------------
; define_type FUNCTION <parameters> -> <result>
;   Types: i32, i64, f32, f64. Use void for no parameters or no result.
;   Example: define_type FUNCTION f64 f64 -> f64
;   Generated symbol: $t_f64_f64__f64. One result at most.
;
; define_import <module> <name> FUNCTION_KIND <type index>
;   Example: define_import env print_i32 FUNCTION_KIND $t_i32__void
;   Generated symbol: $f_env_print_i32.
;
; define_import <module> <name> MEMORY_KIND <flags> <min> [<max>]
;   Example: define_import env memory MEMORY_KIND 0 1
;   Generated symbol: $m_env_memory. Limits are inline, not a memory index.
;
; define_function <type index> <name>
;   Example: define_function $t_void__void main -> $f_main.
;   Function bodies must follow declaration order.
;
; define_memory <flags> <min> [<max>] <name>
;   Example: define_memory 1 1 2 working -> $m_working.
;   Flags 0: minimum only. Flags 1: minimum and maximum.
;   Sizes are 64 KiB pages; 0 <= min <= max <= 65536 when max is supplied.
;   Imported and defined memories are separate. Imported indices come first.
;   Shared memory and memory64 are not supported by these directives.
;
; define_export <name> FUNCTION_KIND <function index>
; define_export <name> MEMORY_KIND <memory index>
;   Export names must be unique across all kinds.
;
; define_code none
; define_code <type> <parameter name> [<type> <parameter name> ...]
;   Follow with define_locals none, or:
;   define_locals <type> <local name> [<type> <local name> ...]
;   Finish with code_end. It writes the function's final end opcode.
;   Use end only for nested blocks/loops/ifs inside a DEFINE body.
;   Locals follow parameters and preserve source order, including mixed types.
;
; define_data active <offset> STRING "text"
; define_data active <offset> STRING_NT "text"
; define_data active <offset> DATA <length> <raw bytes>
;   STRING_NT includes a trailing zero. Active segments target memory 0.
;   For passive segments, use passive instead of active and OMIT the offset:
;   define_data passive STRING "text"
;
; Encoding and compatibility
; --------------------------
; Start sections with SECTION SECTION_<kind>; end them with SECTION_END.
; Order: TYPE, IMPORT, FUNCTION, MEMORY, EXPORT, CODE, DATA.
; DEFINE entries count themselves: do not add COUNT or a raw count for them.
; Keep sections either DEFINE-based or raw. Empty vectors encode a zero count.
; SECTION_CUSTOM selects ID 0; its name and payload are still written raw.
; Raw FUNCTION_START / FUNCTION_END and byte-writing keywords still work.
; Symbols store unsigned 32-bit values. i32.const uses their 32-bit pattern;
; i64.const zero-extends that value. Full-width i64 symbols are not supported.
; Decimal symbol definitions reject overflow instead of silently wrapping.
;
; Added state (four-byte slots in unused parser workspace)
; -------------------------------------------------------
; IMPORT_FUNCTION_COUNT         Next imported function index.
; IMPORT_MEMORY_COUNT           Next imported memory index.
; LOCAL_VARIABLE_COUNT          Next parameter/local index in the body.
; FUNCTION_SYMBOL_NAMES_START   Saved name-stack position.
; FUNCTION_SYMBOL_VALUES_START  Saved value-stack position.
; FUNCTION_SYMBOL_ID_START      Saved symbol ID at function entry.
; PARSED_VALUE                  Result of checked unsigned operand parsing.
; DEFINE_BODY_ACTIVE            Whether a DEFINE body is open.
; DEFINE_LOCALS_EXPECTED        Whether its local declarations are pending.
; Existing buffers, WASI imports, and the 164-page memory size are unchanged.
;
; Added and updated functions
; ---------------------------
; handle_defines_type/import/function/export/memory/data/code/locals:
;   Consume directives, generate symbols, and write their binary entries.
; write_memory_limits: validate and emit shared memory-limit syntax.
; add_variable_properties_from_defines: reserve a checked symbol-name entry.
; add_variable_properties_name_from_defines: copy the symbol's name bytes.
; add_variable_value_from_defines: append its value and advance the symbol ID.
; equals15: recognize define_function.
; skipTrivia, token_end, value_type: scan comments, names, and numeric types.
; append_name, findVariable: construct and locate ordinary symbols.
; read_unsigned: read decimal or symbol operands with 32-bit bounds checks.
; getVariableMode, writePositive64: encode integer-constant symbols correctly.
; parseWord/parseCmd: dispatch the new syntax and close scoped function bodies.
; setVariable/getVariable: support reassignment and preserve raw index output.
; writeSection: include zero vector counts and correct body/section lengths.
; error: report errors 0x0B..0x12 with DEFINE syntax and CUSTOM section names.
; New diagnostics use s_idsuw_start, s_define_*_end, and s_ois_CUSTOM.


; code below:

; Version 1.1 parser state (zero initialized).
